  "summary": "Four documents directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles to energy (electricity consumption) forecasting. [V0133] (Adebayo et al., 2026) uses boosted decision-tree ensembles on the GridWatch dataset, reporting AUROC 0.73. [V0135] (Chen et al., 2019) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles on the FireScope dataset, achieving accuracy 0.87. [V0134] (Brennan et al., 2018) evaluates boosted decision-tree ensembles on ProtMap, reporting F1=0.80. [V0136] (Duarte et al., 2020) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles on ChurnBench, obtaining MAE 0.94. These four constitute the directly relevant set. A fifth slot is filled by [V0126] (Haddad et al., 2025), which addresses electricity consumption prediction but uses self-attention encoder models rather than gradient boosted trees, making it the closest adjacent document; it is ranked fifth as a partial match on topic only. Documents mentioning boosted trees only in prior-work sentences (e.g., V0099, V0073, V0049, V0041, V0034) are excluded as non-applications.",
